@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
actor Player
participant GridWorld as World
participant ClassSpellEffects as Effects
participant SummonRules as Summons
participant "actors: Array[GridActor]" as Actors
participant SaveCodec as Save
Player -> World : cast summon (normal cancellable cast boundaries)
World -> Effects : can_apply / resolve at completion
Effects -> Summons : placement(world, skill)
alt No legal adjacent tile
  Summons --> World : Reject; preserve mana and existing summon
else Legal placement (same-element totem tile may be reused)
  Effects -> Summons : summon(world, skill)
  Summons -> Actors : Remove prior slot; append new actor
  Summons -> Summons : Refresh aura contributions
end
Player -> World : Pet Attack / Stop-Follow / Dismiss
World -> Summons : command(world, id, target)
Summons -> Actors : Validate / update target or remove pet
World --> Player : No simulation time
Player -> World : Commit move / wait / cast boundary
World -> Actors : Expire totems before occupancy / aggro decisions
loop Existing stable actor order
  alt Enemy
    World -> Summons : enemy_target(world, actor)
    Summons --> World : Player or living summon by threat
    World -> Actors : Normal pursuit / melee / damage
  else Pet or totem
    World -> Summons : act(world, actor)
    Summons -> Actors : Follow / cast / swing / pulse if ready
  end
end
World -> Summons : Refresh buffs / auras / caps
World --> Player : Updated resources, messages and sprites
Player -> Save : Save outside combat at action boundary
Save -> World : Capture actor indexes / timers / RNG / learned ranks
note right of Save
Load validates an independent world.
Loop death removes active summons,
retaining all learned ranks.
end note
@enduml
